# Swamp Thing, the April head (ticket 45): a lumpy head of wet dark mud with a heavy brow, a flat nose and a wide black mouth slit with
# stumps of teeth, glowing yellow eyes (emission) deep in their sockets, clumps of moss on the crown, side and back with strands hanging,
# two reeds growing from the top (the slime drips were removed in user review 2).
# Frame (the soldier's head_top socket, ticket 43): the origin is the socket, 1.815 m over the soles; the head faces +Z, +Y is up. The
# size and the height come from the head part (content/parts/swamp_head.sdf): normalized to the common size, the chin 4 cm lower than
# phase 1's (at 1.525 m, over the neck's top at 1.569 whose stub is inside it). The head turns on the Head bone, 0.25 m under the origin.
# The eyes are part of the head (a glowing ellipsoid in each socket), no eye part.
format 1

# No collider (the hit shape of the head is a number in the registry), and never culled before 200 m: the head is what reads at range
collider none
cull 200

Detail detail=0.711
    Part part=swamp_head
